### 1. Create a website widget for an agent
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ai-agents/1/widgets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

{
  "name": "Bosh sahifa ovozli yordamchi",
  "enabled": true,
  "allowedOrigins": ["https://example.uz", "https://www.example.uz"],
  "theme": {
    "primaryColor": "#2F6BFF",
    "position": "BOTTOM_RIGHT"
  },
  "consentRequired": true,
  "consentText": "Ushbu ovozli suhbat sifatni yaxshilash uchun yozib olinadi."
}

### 2. List an agent's widgets
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ai-agents/1/widgets
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 3. Get one widget (response carries the embed snippet)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/widgets/1
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 4. Update a widget
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/widgets/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

{
  "name": "Bosh sahifa ovozli yordamchi (v2)",
  "allowedOrigins": ["https://example.uz"],
  "enabled": true
}

### 5. Delete a widget
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/widgets/1
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 6. Public config — what the embed script reads. No token; the Origin header is
### checked against the widget's allowed-origins list.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/public/widgets/wgt_0123456789abcdef/config
Origin: https://example.uz

### 7. Public session — what the embed script calls when the visitor presses the button.
### No token; the Origin header is checked against the widget's allowed-origins list, and
### the agent's daily/concurrent limits are applied. The response is single-use and the
### session expires in 5 minutes if the browser never dials in.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/public/widgets/wgt_0123456789abcdef/session?language=uz-UZ
Origin: https://example.uz

### 8. The embed snippet itself, for reference — this is what a customer pastes:
###
###   <script src="http://localhost:8080/widgets/v1/widget.js"
###           data-widget-key="wgt_0123456789abcdef" async></script>
###
### Optional attributes:
###   data-api-base   API origin, when the script is served from a CDN instead
###   data-language   force a call language (uz-UZ, ru-RU); default is the agent's
###   data-sip-js     self-hosted SIP.js URL, for deployments with no public CDN access
GET http://localhost:8080/widgets/v1/widget.js
